<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Mas plunges into half-year loss, no div.</title>
<headline>Mas plunges into half-year loss, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     43.1 loss   vs 33.2 profit</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   4.34 loss   vs 2.33 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.92 loss   vs 2.75 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.0	   vs none</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   2.42	  vs 0.34</p>
<p>    Turnover		  40.98	 vs 43.79</p>
<p>Full name: Mas Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said they expected to report an operating profit for the second half of the year.</p>
<p>They said the group had taken a strategic decision to reduce its dependence on the South African Post Office and alternative delivery and payment arrangements were being investigated.</p>
<p>Increasing emphasis was also being placed on the direct selling businesses.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
